Central Securities Depositories (CSDs) support the European and international companies by helping them to finance their growth by issuing securities (shares, debt and other financial instruments) and rendering them transferable with full legal certainty on financial markets locally and cross-border.
ECSDA Members are critical financial infrastructures in each European Member State, and are front-running innovation in Europe and globally. ECSDA supports ethical and trusted finance. Our Members use different new and proven technologies to provide services with a high level of risk management and resilience, which addresses the constantly evolving needs of European issuers and investors most diligently and safely.
Your Role
As part of our small and dynamic team, you will actively contribute to ECSDA’s work on:
Preparing meetings of European CSD experts across relevant domains in the areas of cross-border harmonisation and implementation of European reforms and standards, drafting agendas and papers;
Engaging with members, peer associations and authorities to support the creation of a truly single and modern financial market in the EU, and deepening cooperation with the neighbouring EEA States, UK and Switzerland;
Together with national experts engaging with the EU institutions- European Commission, Securities and Markets Authority, as well as the European Central Bank, advocating removal of cross-border barriers, harmonisation of post-trade market practices contributing to further elaboration of pan-European policies, and innovation, including through digitalisation and tokenisation, shortening the securities settlement cycle, enhancing operational efficiency and resilience;
Shaping the European regulatory environment through regular exchanges with the European policy-makers, supporting regulatory compliance and supervisory dialogue;
Analysing the data and researching further possibilities of harmonisation of market infrastructure, development of digital assets and emerging technologies; and
Collaborating with financial market infrastructures and their regional representatives globally.
You will start by supporting senior officers in research, coordination, drafting of position papers and advice to policy-makers and external stakeholders. Shortly, we expect you to learn and evolve to take responsibility for one or more working groups, gaining exposure across European States rarely accessible at an early stage of a career.
Why ECSDA?
A front-row seat to European capital markets policy and market infrastructure Association, representing critical financial infrastructure in all European Markets;
Meaningful responsibilities from day one – you will be able to evolve and take responsibility quickly;
Direct interaction with senior market practitioners, regulators, and EU institutions;
A supportive, international team in the heart of Brussels, of which you will be an essential part.
ECSDA is a high-quality line in your CV and an excellent stepping stone for your career. Our former young professionals have pursued their careers working for ECSDA at a senior level, or accepted an offer within European authorities, permanent representations of EU Member States, CSDs and other financial market actors, or other Trade associations based in Brussels or London.
