The Director, SI PI is responsible for leading a team of bankers, engineers, project managers and technical cooperation (TC) grant managers that enables and amplifies the work of the Bank in the Sustainable Infrastructure sector. The SI PI team delivers three key functions in the sustainable infrastructure sector: (1) managing the Bank’s portfolio of debt investments The Director strives to achieve this by overall oversight of day-to-day portfolio management activities acting as the first line of defence, (2) sourcing, managing and reporting on the use of donor funds for the Bank’s activities, in close cooperation with the Bank’s Donor Partnerships team, and (3) providing technical and engineering advice and support in the design and implementation of the Bank’s activities. The remit of the SI PI team’s work includes the power, energy, transport, social infrastructure and municipal sectors.
Accountabilities & Responsibilities
Process and Business Delivery;
Accountable for the team’s delivery and fulfilment of quantitative and qualitative objectives of the annual scorecard, these objectives support the annual objectives for the Business Group and the annual business plan of the Bank;
Provide strategic direction of activities across all three units of SI PI (Portfolio, Project Preparation and Implementation and TC Grants) to support SIG’s strategic objectives. This requires close cooperation with the rest of the SIG senior leadership team and MD CSG COO as well as frequent interaction with Managing Directors and Directors across ROs, Risk Management, Corporate Recovery, ESD, OCCO, PPAD, Impact and Partnerships and VP3 generally;
Accountable for the delivery of high quality technical and engineering input into both investment and policy dialogue in the sustainable infrastructure sector, including delivery of upstream feasibility studies, support for reform efforts, TC activities, delivering technical due diligence for all investments, both directly and through the supervision of external consultants, supporting procurement and contracting for public sector projects and monitoring and troubleshooting the implementation of projects. Ensure close coordination with bankers and with technical experts covering the same areas in the Policy Strategy and Delivery and Climate Strategy and Delivery teams, including in relation to the Bank’s Green Cities programme;
Accountable for the sourcing, management and reporting on donor funds to support investment and policy dialogue in the sustainable infrastructure sector. Actively contribute to building the Bank’s credibility and profile with donors and participate in relationship management accordingly. Ensure close cooperation with the Donor Partnerships team;
Overall responsibility for monitoring and protecting the reputation, credit quality and impact of the Bank’s sustainable infrastructure loan portfolio. Accountable for the management of the performing loan portfolio, ensuring required processes are in place and being followed to ensure adequate monitoring, so that early signs of borrower issues are captured and actioned on in a timely manner. Oversight and guidance on all potential and active restructuring cases that have not been downgraded below CR2, or those put on the watch-list, and have not been transferred to Risk Management, ensuring application of early and pro-active portfolio management;
Providing general support to SIG and Bank management on sectoral issues and data management for the group as a whole Management;
Responsible for supervision the team’s budget and other non-staff resources in coordination with relevant departments to ensure an efficient and optimum utilisation of resources in compliance with the rules and procedures of the Bank, such as corporate procurement, budget processes, travel and expenses policy, the Staff Handbook;
